WEBVTT

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:04.700
How do you do?

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:11.140
Mr. Carl Lindley feels it would be a little unkind

00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:14.220
to present this picture without just a word of friendly warning.

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:18.660
We are about to unfold the story of Frankenstein,

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:24.600
a man of science who sought to create a man after his own image

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:27.600
without reckoning upon God.

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:32.080
strangest tales ever told.

00:00:33.350 --> 00:00:35.230
It deals with the two great mysteries

00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:38.410
of creation, life and death.

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:43.020
I think it will thrill you. It may

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:45.960
shock you. It might even

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:49.940
horrify you. So if any of you feel that you

00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:51.820
do not care to subject your nerves to such a

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:54.670
strain, now is your chance to

00:00:54.670 --> 00:00:58.110
well, we've warned you.

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:05.040
God bless you!

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:06.160
God bless you!

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:08.760
God bless you!

00:02:09.710 --> 00:02:10.220
Amen!

00:02:35.910 --> 00:02:39.130
I found you.

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:05.810
Thank you.

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:21.630
Now, come on, hurry.

00:04:31.760 --> 00:04:44.360
The moon's rising. We've no time to lose.

00:04:46.460 --> 00:04:46.880
Careful!

00:05:06.940 --> 00:05:09.650
He's just resting, waiting for a new life to come.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:44.700
Here we are. It's still here.

00:05:47.920 --> 00:05:48.880
Climb up and cut the roof.

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:50.720
No.

00:05:51.390 --> 00:05:52.750
Go on. It can't hurt you.

00:05:54.300 --> 00:05:54.820
Here's the knife.

00:06:22.720 --> 00:06:25.350
tonight. I come.

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:31.060
Is it all right?

00:06:32.140 --> 00:06:35.130
The neck's broken. The brain is useless.

00:06:36.720 --> 00:06:38.500
We must find another brain.

00:07:10.650 --> 00:07:16.870
And in conclusion, ladies and gentlemen, here we have one of the most perfect specimens of the human brain

00:07:16.870 --> 00:07:19.310
that has ever come to my attention at the university.

00:07:19.740 --> 00:07:22.380
And here the abnormal brain of the typical criminal.

00:07:23.590 --> 00:07:28.040
Observe, ladies and gentlemen, the scarcity of convolutions on the frontal lobe

00:07:28.510 --> 00:07:29.790
as compared to that of the...

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:35.440
the normal brain and the distinct degeneration of the middle frontal lobe.

00:07:36.520 --> 00:07:41.930
All of these degenerate characteristics check amazingly with the case history of the dead man before us...

00:07:41.930 --> 00:07:46.420
whose life was one of brutality, of violence and murder.

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:49.720
Both of these jars will remain here for your further inspection.

00:07:50.480 --> 00:07:51.760
Thank you, gentlemen. The glass is dismissed.

00:08:00.350 --> 00:08:00.550
Thank you.

00:08:30.540 --> 00:08:31.260
Thank you.

00:09:29.180 --> 00:09:29.580
Thank you, Mr. Morris.

00:09:34.060 --> 00:09:37.160
Victor, I'm so glad you've come.

00:09:37.260 --> 00:09:39.420
What is it, Elizabeth? Oh, you've heard from Henry.

00:09:39.600 --> 00:09:42.790
Yes, the first word in four months. It just came.

00:09:44.650 --> 00:09:45.850
Victor, you must help me.

00:09:45.870 --> 00:09:46.970
Of course I'll help you.

00:09:47.410 --> 00:09:52.360
I'm afraid. I've read this over and over again,

00:09:52.440 --> 00:09:54.750
but they're just words that I can't understand.

00:09:56.410 --> 00:09:59.980
Listen, you must have faith in me, Elizabeth. Wait.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:06.160
my work must come first even before you at night the winds howl in the mountains

00:10:06.160 --> 00:10:13.410
there's no one here prying eyes can't peer into my secret what can he mean what

00:10:14.070 --> 00:10:20.110
does he say then I am living in an abandoned old watchtower close to the

00:10:20.110 --> 00:10:25.270
town of Goldstadt only my assistant is here to help me with my experiments oh

00:10:25.970 --> 00:10:28.970
his experiments yes that's what frightens me

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:32.460
Every day we announced our engagement, he told me of his experiments.

00:10:33.640 --> 00:10:37.140
He said he was on the verge of a discovery so terrific that he doubted his own sanity.

00:10:38.260 --> 00:10:41.540
There was a strange look in his eyes, some mystery.

00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:43.980
His words carried me right away.

00:10:44.320 --> 00:10:48.400
Of course, I've never doubted him, but still I worry, I can't help it.

00:10:49.740 --> 00:10:50.680
No, that's better.

00:10:51.550 --> 00:10:53.790
This uncertainty can't go on, I must know.

00:10:54.340 --> 00:10:56.400
Victor, have you seen him?

00:10:56.860 --> 00:10:59.170
Yes, about three weeks ago.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:04.210
walking alone in the woods. He spoke to me of his work too. I asked him if I might

00:11:04.210 --> 00:11:08.370
visit his laboratory. He just glared at me and said he'd let no one go there.

00:11:09.120 --> 00:11:14.980
His manner was very strange. Oh, what can we do? Oh, we should be ill. Now, don't worry.

00:11:15.730 --> 00:11:19.770
I'll go to Dr. Waldman, Henry's old professor in medical school. Perhaps he

00:11:19.770 --> 00:11:24.960
can tell me more about all this. Victor, your idea. You know I'd go to the

00:11:24.960 --> 00:11:29.340
ends of the earth for you. I shouldn't like that. I'm far too fond of you.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:30.700
I wish you were.

00:11:33.720 --> 00:11:34.080
Victor.

00:11:35.090 --> 00:11:35.650
I'm sorry.

00:11:40.690 --> 00:11:41.870
Good night, Victor, and thank you.

00:11:42.370 --> 00:11:42.870
Thank you.

00:11:43.070 --> 00:11:45.100
Good night, and don't worry.

00:11:45.710 --> 00:11:45.990
Promise?

00:11:46.920 --> 00:11:47.440
I won't.

00:11:54.120 --> 00:11:55.370
What is it?

00:11:58.070 --> 00:11:58.710
I'm coming with you.

00:11:58.790 --> 00:11:59.970
But Elizabeth, you can't do that!

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:02.180
I must. I'll be ready in a minute.

00:12:07.520 --> 00:12:09.820
Herr Frankenstein is a most brilliant young man.

00:12:10.340 --> 00:12:12.880
Yet so erratic, he troubles me.

00:12:14.140 --> 00:12:17.160
I'm worried about Henry. Why has he left the university?

00:12:17.930 --> 00:12:21.720
He was doing so well and he seemed so happy with his work.

00:12:22.930 --> 00:12:26.730
Well, you know his research is in the field of chemical galvanism and electro-biology.

00:12:27.200 --> 00:12:29.500
We're far in advance of our theories here at the university.

00:12:31.020 --> 00:12:33.180
In fact, they had reached a most advanced stage.

00:12:33.870 --> 00:12:35.350
They were becoming dangerous.

00:12:37.450 --> 00:12:39.510
Herr Frankenstein is greatly changed.

00:12:39.650 --> 00:12:41.670
You mean changed as a result of his work?

00:12:42.300 --> 00:12:43.560
Yes, his work.

00:12:44.330 --> 00:12:46.450
His insane ambition to create life.

00:12:48.370 --> 00:12:49.920
How? How?

00:12:52.520 --> 00:12:54.340
Please tell us everything, whatever it is.

00:12:55.180 --> 00:12:58.220
The bodies we use in our dissecting room for lecture purposes...

00:12:58.430 --> 00:12:59.970
...were not perfect enough for his experience.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:05.660
he said. He wished us to supply him with other bodies and we were not to be too

00:13:05.660 --> 00:13:10.950
particular as to where and how we got. I told him that his demands were

00:13:10.950 --> 00:13:16.380
unreasonable and so he left the university to work on Hample, found what

00:13:16.380 --> 00:13:20.800
he needed elsewhere. Oh, the bodies of animals. Well, what are the lives of a few

00:13:20.800 --> 00:13:27.290
rabbits and dogs? You do not quite get what I mean. Herr Frankenstein was

00:13:27.290 --> 00:13:28.790
interested only in human life.

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:32.850
First to destroy it, then recreate it.

00:13:33.860 --> 00:13:36.260
There you have his mad dream.

00:13:40.270 --> 00:13:40.910
Can we go to him?

00:13:41.740 --> 00:13:42.880
You will not be very welcome.

00:13:43.200 --> 00:13:44.140
Oh, what does that matter?

00:13:44.610 --> 00:13:45.630
I must see him.

00:13:46.610 --> 00:13:47.410
Dr. Verdmann.

00:13:48.090 --> 00:13:49.330
You have influence with Henry.

00:13:50.220 --> 00:13:51.080
Won't you come with us?

00:13:51.820 --> 00:13:54.360
I am sorry, but Herr Frankenstein is no longer my pupil.

00:13:56.060 --> 00:13:57.120
But he respects you.

00:13:58.720 --> 00:13:59.980
Won't you help us to take him away?

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:05.650
Very well, Fräulein. I've warned you, but if you wish it, I will go.

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:30.180
It!

00:14:31.110 --> 00:14:31.630
Hello.

00:14:34.100 --> 00:14:35.480
Finish making those connections.

00:14:36.910 --> 00:14:37.130
We can.

00:14:37.510 --> 00:14:38.750
Well, come down then.

00:14:39.440 --> 00:14:41.280
We hope that his attention will be lost to Duke.

00:15:12.990 --> 00:15:19.390
develops as I hope. We'll have plenty to be afraid of before the night's over. Go on, fix the electrodes.

00:15:32.040 --> 00:15:33.480
This storm will be magnificent.

00:15:34.690 --> 00:15:36.470
All the electrical secrets of heaven.

00:15:38.370 --> 00:15:39.450
This time we're ready.

00:15:39.900 --> 00:15:40.480
Eh, Fritz?

00:15:41.280 --> 00:15:41.600
Ready.

00:15:42.300 --> 00:15:46.920
What's the matter?

00:15:47.400 --> 00:15:51.870
Look! There's nothing to fear.

00:15:52.730 --> 00:15:56.360
Look, no blood, no decay.

00:15:57.780 --> 00:15:58.700
Just a few stitches.

00:16:01.470 --> 00:16:04.190
And look, here's the final touch.

00:16:08.950 --> 00:16:11.930
Brain you stole, Fritz. Think of it.

00:16:12.590 --> 00:16:18.280
Brain of a dead man waiting to live again in a body I made with my own hands.

00:16:19.340 --> 00:16:20.640
With my own hands?

00:16:24.480 --> 00:16:26.750
Let's have one final test. Throw the switches.

00:16:46.830 --> 00:16:50.560
minutes the storm should be at its height. Then we'll be ready.

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:06.250
Send them away! Nobody must come here!

00:17:08.250 --> 00:17:08.530
Here!

00:17:09.760 --> 00:17:26.200
Leave them to me!

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:31.360
It's time for anybody to come.

00:17:31.760 --> 00:17:35.800
Now, let me...

00:17:37.820 --> 00:17:39.660
You're messing about at this time of night.

00:17:39.880 --> 00:17:40.900
Got too much to do.

00:17:43.180 --> 00:17:49.990
It's all right. It's all development vids.

00:17:50.110 --> 00:17:51.750
You can't see it. Go away.

00:18:41.450 --> 00:18:59.600
You must leave me alone, please. Won't you go away? Won't you trust me just for tonight?

00:19:00.280 --> 00:19:00.780
What's the matter?

00:19:01.000 --> 00:19:01.300
Nothing.

00:19:01.660 --> 00:19:02.880
I'm quite all right.

00:19:03.330 --> 00:19:04.150
Truly, I am.

00:19:04.710 --> 00:19:05.570
Oh, can't you see?

00:19:05.710 --> 00:19:06.670
I mustn't be disturbed.

00:19:07.200 --> 00:19:08.340
You'll ruin everything.

00:19:09.010 --> 00:19:10.950
My experiment is almost completed.

00:19:11.440 --> 00:19:11.880
Wait a moment.

00:19:12.720 --> 00:19:13.380
I understand.

00:19:13.480 --> 00:19:15.280
I believe in you.

00:19:15.400 --> 00:19:17.760
But I cannot leave you tonight.

00:19:18.120 --> 00:19:19.780
You're not the only thing, Henry.

00:19:19.920 --> 00:19:20.560
You're inhuman.

00:19:20.840 --> 00:19:21.720
You're crazy.

00:19:23.140 --> 00:19:24.080
Crazy am I.

00:19:24.360 --> 00:19:28.100
You'll see whether I'm crazy or not.

00:19:32.780 --> 00:19:50.780
Come on up, sure you want to come in?

00:20:17.720 --> 00:20:19.640
I'm forced to take unusual precautions.

00:20:24.540 --> 00:20:25.520
Sit down, please.

00:20:28.520 --> 00:20:29.280
Sit down!

00:20:35.150 --> 00:20:37.690
You too, Elizabeth, please.

00:20:41.540 --> 00:20:44.360
A moment ago, you said I was crazy.

00:20:45.660 --> 00:20:47.160
Tomorrow we'll see about that.

00:20:47.340 --> 00:20:48.240
Don't touch that!

00:20:49.180 --> 00:20:56.750
Sorry, Doctor, but I insist.

00:21:02.200 --> 00:21:29.700
Dr. Waldman, I learned a great deal from you at the university about the violet ray, the ultraviolet ray, which you said was the highest color in the spectrum. You were wrong.

00:21:31.660 --> 00:21:34.850
Here in this machinery, I have gone beyond that.

00:21:37.800 --> 00:21:42.060
I have discovered the great ray that first brought life into the world.

00:21:42.340 --> 00:21:44.130
Oh, and your proof?

00:21:45.300 --> 00:21:47.200
Tonight you shall have your proof.

00:21:49.670 --> 00:21:52.170
First I experimented only with dead animals,

00:21:53.100 --> 00:21:56.760
and then a human heart which I kept beating for three weeks.

00:21:58.690 --> 00:21:59.250
Now...

00:22:00.380 --> 00:22:05.290
I'm going to turn that ray on that body and endow it with life.

00:22:06.260 --> 00:22:09.320
And you really believe that you can bring life to the dead?

00:22:10.520 --> 00:22:12.360
That body is not dead.

00:22:13.100 --> 00:22:14.220
It has never lived.

00:22:16.070 --> 00:22:17.270
I created it.

00:22:17.880 --> 00:22:23.360
I made it with my own hands from the bodies I took from graves, from the gallows, anywhere.

00:22:23.500 --> 00:22:28.650
Go and see for yourself.

00:22:30.190 --> 00:22:55.420
He, one man crazy, he, very same spectators.

00:25:01.630 --> 00:25:07.230
It's alive! It's alive, Luke! It's alive! It's alive! It's alive!

00:25:07.350 --> 00:25:13.560
In the name of God, I'd like to be God!

00:25:26.420 --> 00:25:29.530
Well, but he's very busy. He said he would get in touch with you soon.

00:25:30.440 --> 00:25:33.470
Don't worry about him, Baron. He'll be home in a few days.

00:25:34.450 --> 00:25:36.550
You two have it all arranged, haven't you?

00:25:37.520 --> 00:25:38.980
You think I'm an idiot, don't you?

00:25:39.530 --> 00:25:40.210
But I'm not.

00:25:42.140 --> 00:25:44.720
Anyone can see with half an eye there's something wrong.

00:25:45.600 --> 00:25:48.070
And I've two eyes. Pretty good ones as that.

00:25:48.740 --> 00:25:49.540
Well, what is it?

00:25:49.810 --> 00:25:50.990
You're quite mistaken, Baron.

00:25:51.790 --> 00:25:53.710
What's the matter with my son? What's he doing?

00:25:55.010 --> 00:25:56.790
Completing his experiments, that's all.

00:25:57.070 --> 00:25:59.910
Why does he go messing around an old windmill?

00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:04.280
when he has a decent house, a bath, good food and drink,

00:26:04.870 --> 00:26:06.850
and a darn pretty girl to come back to.

00:26:07.390 --> 00:26:08.640
Will you tell me that?

00:26:09.260 --> 00:26:10.560
Baron, you don't understand.

00:26:10.760 --> 00:26:12.080
I understand perfectly well.

00:26:12.960 --> 00:26:15.740
There's another woman, and you're afraid to tell me.

00:26:16.470 --> 00:26:18.670
Pretty sort of experiments these must be.

00:26:19.190 --> 00:26:20.450
Oh, but you're wrong.

00:26:20.830 --> 00:26:21.790
And how do you know?

00:26:22.260 --> 00:26:25.030
If you please, Herr Baron, the Burgermaster.

00:26:25.720 --> 00:26:27.760
Well, tell him to go away.

00:26:28.040 --> 00:26:29.180
But he says it's important.

00:26:29.500 --> 00:26:29.980
Nothing that...

00:26:30.060 --> 00:26:32.920
What Burgermaster can say can be of the slightest importance.

00:26:35.070 --> 00:26:36.090
Good day, Herr Baron.

00:26:37.180 --> 00:26:37.620
Freulein?

00:26:38.320 --> 00:26:39.460
Well, what do you want?

00:26:40.350 --> 00:26:41.850
If it's trouble, go away.

00:26:42.260 --> 00:26:43.160
I've trouble enough.

00:26:43.730 --> 00:26:44.770
Oh, there's no trouble, sir.

00:26:45.100 --> 00:26:46.360
What do you mean, no trouble?

00:26:46.900 --> 00:26:48.000
There's nothing but trouble.

00:26:48.940 --> 00:26:50.440
I brought you these flowers.

00:26:51.130 --> 00:26:52.110
Thank you, Herr Vogel.

00:26:53.400 --> 00:26:56.540
Both in my private and official capacities as Burgermaster.

00:26:56.880 --> 00:26:59.960
Yes, yes, yes, yes, we know all about that, but what do you...

00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:04.740
Well, what I really want to know is, when will the wedding be, if you please?

00:27:05.220 --> 00:27:09.140
Unless Henry comes to his senses, there'll be no wedding at all.

00:27:09.830 --> 00:27:12.110
But, Herr Baron, the village is already prepared.

00:27:12.350 --> 00:27:13.750
Well, tell him to unprepare.

00:27:14.300 --> 00:27:19.800
Oh, but such a lovely bride, such a fine young man, the very image of his father.

00:27:19.900 --> 00:27:20.620
Heaven forbid.

00:27:21.090 --> 00:27:23.070
But, sir, everything is ready.

00:27:23.210 --> 00:27:25.950
I know that. Don't keep on saying so, you idiot.

00:27:27.090 --> 00:27:28.590
There's nothing to cry about.

00:27:29.230 --> 00:27:29.970
Good day, man.

00:27:30.720 --> 00:27:32.160
Good day, Herr Moritz.

00:27:33.050 --> 00:27:34.490
Good day, Herr Vogel.

00:27:36.490 --> 00:27:37.670
Good day, Herr Baron.

00:27:39.670 --> 00:27:40.630
Good riddance to you.

00:27:41.950 --> 00:27:42.730
There you are.

00:27:43.130 --> 00:27:44.680
You see how it is?

00:27:45.300 --> 00:27:46.960
The whole village is kept waiting,

00:27:47.560 --> 00:27:48.920
the bride is kept waiting,

00:27:49.600 --> 00:27:51.610
and I am kept waiting.

00:27:52.500 --> 00:27:54.920
Henry must come home if I have to fetch him myself.

00:27:55.060 --> 00:27:55.620
No, no, Baron.

00:27:55.760 --> 00:27:56.640
What do you mean, no, no?

00:27:56.780 --> 00:27:57.440
What about his work?

00:27:57.700 --> 00:27:58.400
Stuff and nonsense.

00:27:58.600 --> 00:27:59.400
What about his wedding?

00:28:00.280 --> 00:28:04.580
There is another woman, and I'm going to find her.

00:28:17.930 --> 00:28:19.450
Come and sit down, Doctor.

00:28:20.660 --> 00:28:21.940
You must be patient.

00:28:22.900 --> 00:28:24.560
Do you expect perfection at once?

00:28:25.590 --> 00:28:28.550
This creature of yours should be kept under guard.

00:28:29.150 --> 00:28:29.890
Mark my word.

00:28:30.640 --> 00:28:31.540
You will prove dangerous.

00:28:33.520 --> 00:28:34.000
Dangerous?

00:28:35.610 --> 00:28:36.510
Poor old Balmain.

00:28:40.730 --> 00:28:43.170
Have you never wanted to do anything that was dangerous?

00:28:44.510 --> 00:28:47.630
Where should we be if nobody tried to find out what lies beyond?

00:28:48.720 --> 00:28:51.920
You never wanted to look beyond the clouds and the stars?

00:28:52.680 --> 00:28:54.740
Or to know what causes the trees to bud?

00:28:55.700 --> 00:28:57.880
And what changes the darkness into light?

00:29:01.240 --> 00:29:04.510
But if you talk like that, people call you crazy.

00:29:07.700 --> 00:29:10.660
Well, if I could discover just one of these things,

00:29:11.720 --> 00:29:13.220
what eternity is, for example,

00:29:14.530 --> 00:29:17.880
I wouldn't care if they did think I was crazy.

00:29:18.940 --> 00:29:20.080
You're young, my friend.

00:29:20.720 --> 00:29:22.180
Your success has intoxicated you.

00:29:22.740 --> 00:29:25.240
Wake up and look facts in the face.

00:29:26.470 --> 00:29:28.910
Here we have a fiend whose brain...

00:29:28.910 --> 00:29:29.970
Whose brain must be...

00:29:32.100 --> 00:29:33.880
It's a perfectly good brain, Doctor.

00:29:35.120 --> 00:29:38.060
Well, you ought to know. It came from your own laboratory.

00:29:39.350 --> 00:29:43.690
The brain that was stolen from my laboratory was a criminal brain.

00:29:54.660 --> 00:29:56.460
After all, it's only a piece of dead tissue.

00:29:57.460 --> 00:29:59.180
Only evil can come of it.

00:30:00.000 --> 00:30:02.620
Your health will be ruined if you persist in this madness.

00:30:02.880 --> 00:30:04.840
I'm astonishingly sane, Doctor.

00:30:05.730 --> 00:30:08.830
You have created a monster and it will destroy you.

00:30:09.590 --> 00:30:10.590
Patience, patience.

00:30:11.960 --> 00:30:14.420
I believe in this monster, as you call it.

00:30:15.080 --> 00:30:17.180
And if you don't, well, you must leave me alone.

00:30:18.220 --> 00:30:20.180
But think of Elizabeth, your father.

00:30:20.940 --> 00:30:22.320
Elizabeth believes in me.

00:30:23.180 --> 00:30:25.720
My father never believes in anyone.

00:30:28.230 --> 00:30:29.910
I've got to experiment first.

00:30:31.050 --> 00:30:32.750
He's only a few days old, remember.

00:30:33.690 --> 00:30:36.090
So far, he's been kept in complete darkness.

00:30:37.400 --> 00:30:38.900
Wait till I bring him into the light.

00:30:45.490 --> 00:30:48.190
Here he comes. Let's turn out the light.

00:31:30.090 --> 00:31:55.110
Come in, down.

00:32:02.490 --> 00:32:06.050
You see, it understands. Watch.

00:32:50.890 --> 00:32:51.970
There, Frankenstein, take care.

00:32:57.780 --> 00:32:58.320
Get out the light.

00:33:17.760 --> 00:33:22.400
Go and sit down.

00:33:42.280 --> 00:33:44.160
It understands this time. It's wonderful.

00:33:44.500 --> 00:33:47.000
Frankenstein! Frankenstein! Where is it? Where is it?

00:33:48.140 --> 00:33:54.290
Quiet, you fool! Get away with that torture!

00:34:18.040 --> 00:34:19.640
Shoot it! It's a monster!

00:34:34.730 --> 00:34:34.990
Quiet!

00:34:43.380 --> 00:34:43.820
Quiet on us!

00:34:45.440 --> 00:34:45.760
Go away!

00:34:45.900 --> 00:34:47.120
He has to spend such ten minutes!

00:34:50.160 --> 00:34:50.460
Give me that!

00:34:53.750 --> 00:34:56.330
Leave it alone!

00:35:08.250 --> 00:35:08.490
Thank you.

00:36:25.970 --> 00:36:27.840
Oh, it's tormenting him.

00:36:31.560 --> 00:36:33.480
Come, come, pull yourself together.

00:36:33.680 --> 00:36:34.680
What can we do?

00:36:34.900 --> 00:36:35.260
Kill it.

00:36:35.630 --> 00:36:36.810
As you would any savage animal.

00:36:37.310 --> 00:36:38.630
We must overpower him first.

00:36:38.960 --> 00:36:39.980
Get me a hypodermic needle.

00:36:40.420 --> 00:36:41.080
It's murder.

00:36:41.160 --> 00:36:42.200
It's our only chance.

00:36:42.620 --> 00:36:44.080
In a few minutes he'll be through that door.

00:36:44.300 --> 00:36:45.220
Come, quick, hurry.

00:36:58.130 --> 00:36:59.260
Yes, there it is.

00:37:00.000 --> 00:37:01.910
It's very strong. Half grain solution.

00:37:02.110 --> 00:37:05.110
Good. Now then, you stand there.

00:37:05.660 --> 00:37:07.980
When he goes toward you, I will leave the injection in his back.

00:37:10.620 --> 00:37:11.480
Ready? Yes.

00:37:32.640 --> 00:37:33.960
Hey!

00:37:40.540 --> 00:37:41.220
Hey!

00:37:42.060 --> 00:37:42.240
Hey!

00:38:02.770 --> 00:38:16.420
Dr. Varmann, are you hurt?

00:38:16.910 --> 00:38:18.110
No, no, I'm all right, it's nothing.

00:38:18.940 --> 00:38:19.760
See who's at the door.

00:38:23.960 --> 00:38:24.940
What's happening here?

00:38:25.500 --> 00:38:27.580
Elizabeth and your father are coming up the hill to see you.

00:38:27.680 --> 00:38:28.480
You must keep him out!

00:38:28.700 --> 00:38:29.000
Too late!

00:38:29.120 --> 00:38:29.900
They must not see that!

00:38:30.000 --> 00:38:32.000
Here, quick, get me ahead! Quick!

00:38:35.860 --> 00:38:50.470
Henry, hurry upstairs and get that blood off your face

00:38:50.470 --> 00:38:51.950
before your father and Elizabeth get here.

00:39:01.180 --> 00:39:05.660
Well, it's a pretty sort of place for my son to be in, I must say.

00:39:07.060 --> 00:39:08.040
Is that the front door?

00:39:08.900 --> 00:39:09.780
Yes, this is it.

00:39:10.380 --> 00:39:15.220
Well, I don't like it, but here it goes.

00:39:21.500 --> 00:39:23.600
There doesn't seem to be anybody in the place, son.

00:39:24.680 --> 00:39:25.060
Go off!

00:39:33.480 --> 00:39:36.520
What a... what a forsaken place here.

00:39:37.080 --> 00:39:39.700
You're trying to burn it down, eh? What's that for, eh?

00:39:39.780 --> 00:39:41.570
Well, what's the matter with you?

00:39:42.090 --> 00:39:43.990
You look as if you've been kicked by a horse.

00:39:44.680 --> 00:39:45.300
Where's Henry?

00:39:45.840 --> 00:39:46.120
Why?

00:39:46.490 --> 00:39:46.850
Well?

00:39:47.540 --> 00:39:49.020
He can't be disturbed just now.

00:39:49.100 --> 00:39:49.740
Oh, can't he?

00:39:50.020 --> 00:39:50.200
Heh!

00:39:50.540 --> 00:39:51.780
I'll soon settle that nonsense.

00:39:52.500 --> 00:39:53.360
Victor, where is he?

00:39:53.740 --> 00:39:56.040
This place seems to drive everybody crazy.

00:39:56.480 --> 00:39:56.960
I...

00:39:57.170 --> 00:39:58.710
What... what's that?

00:39:59.210 --> 00:39:59.670
I...

00:40:00.120 --> 00:40:02.420
I beg your pardon. I am Dr. Valdner.

00:40:02.580 --> 00:40:05.340
Oh, are you? I'm Baron Frankenstein.

00:40:05.960 --> 00:40:08.920
Perhaps you know what all this tommy rot's about.

00:40:10.240 --> 00:40:11.440
I'd be shocked if I do.

00:40:12.080 --> 00:40:14.320
I would advise you to take Henry away from here at once.

00:40:14.520 --> 00:40:16.520
What do you suppose I'm here for? Pleasure?

00:40:16.960 --> 00:40:17.940
What? Nah.

00:40:19.020 --> 00:40:21.120
Where are you, my dear? Oh, there you are.

00:40:21.400 --> 00:40:23.380
Let's go and see what's up to awful stairs.

00:40:23.640 --> 00:40:25.580
I don't know how the deuce I'd better get up a little.

00:40:27.940 --> 00:40:29.140
Why do you want to be a brute?

00:40:30.000 --> 00:40:31.500
Leave them alone.

00:40:36.010 --> 00:40:39.410
Come here.

00:40:43.000 --> 00:40:43.280
Henry.

00:40:48.620 --> 00:40:55.630
Dear, what have they done to you?

00:40:58.160 --> 00:40:59.840
Get him off the sofa.

00:41:10.830 --> 00:41:17.100
You got any brandy? Quick, quick, quick, quick.

00:41:19.740 --> 00:41:27.040
Can I do that? My boy, now. Now drink. Drink, please.

00:41:30.000 --> 00:41:32.250
There, there, that's better.

00:41:33.070 --> 00:41:34.970
I'm going to take you home with me, Henry.

00:41:35.760 --> 00:41:37.380
No, I can't. My work.

00:41:38.060 --> 00:41:40.040
What will happen to the records of my experiment?

00:41:40.260 --> 00:41:41.260
We will preserve them.

00:41:41.480 --> 00:41:42.320
And Helen...

00:41:42.340 --> 00:41:44.420
I will see that it is painlessly destroyed.

00:41:44.890 --> 00:41:46.550
Yes, yes, leave it all to me.

00:41:47.350 --> 00:41:49.930
Poor Francis. Poor my father.

00:41:50.010 --> 00:41:51.730
There, Henry, you can't do any more now.

00:41:52.050 --> 00:41:54.120
You must come home until you get well again.

00:41:55.140 --> 00:41:57.020
You'll soon feel better when you get out of here.

00:44:09.020 --> 00:44:10.540
It's like heaven being with you again.

00:44:11.960 --> 00:44:14.100
Heaven wasn't so far away all the time, you know.

00:44:14.410 --> 00:44:16.980
I know, but I didn't realize it.

00:44:18.350 --> 00:44:21.750
My work, those horrible days and nights.

00:44:23.260 --> 00:44:24.500
I couldn't think of anything else.

00:44:25.060 --> 00:44:28.090
Henry, you're not to think of those things anymore.

00:44:29.100 --> 00:44:29.680
You promised.

00:44:30.480 --> 00:44:34.670
All right. Let's think about us. When will our wedding be?

00:44:38.110 --> 00:44:39.110
Let's make it soon.

00:44:40.140 --> 00:44:41.240
As soon as you like.

00:44:50.840 --> 00:44:56.240
For three generations, these orange blossoms have been worn at our wedding.

00:44:57.510 --> 00:44:59.450
Your great-grandfather wore this, Henry.

00:45:00.030 --> 00:45:03.260
Looks as good as new now, eh?

00:45:04.020 --> 00:45:08.440
And here, here's one to make the best man look still better.

00:45:08.660 --> 00:45:09.160
Thank you, sir.

00:45:09.700 --> 00:45:14.890
Thirty years ago, I placed this on your mother's head, Henry.

00:45:16.380 --> 00:45:20.350
Today, you will make me very happy by doing the same for Elizabeth.

00:45:20.810 --> 00:45:24.070
And I hope, I hope in thirty years' time,

00:45:24.480 --> 00:45:26.740
a youngster of yours will be carrying on the tradition.

00:45:28.140 --> 00:45:29.960
And now, now, how...

00:45:30.000 --> 00:45:31.280
How about a little drink, eh?

00:45:31.520 --> 00:45:32.080
Come on.

00:45:33.840 --> 00:45:36.800
My grandfather bought this wine and laid it down.

00:45:38.360 --> 00:45:40.840
My grandmother wouldn't let him drink it.

00:45:41.440 --> 00:45:44.140
Bless her heart. Here's to a very good health.

00:45:45.730 --> 00:45:48.100
You all full? Yes, come along.

00:45:48.690 --> 00:45:52.820
Here's a health to a son of the house of Frankenstein.

00:45:53.050 --> 00:45:55.350
A son to the house of Frankenstein.

00:45:57.230 --> 00:45:59.970
Here's a jolly good health to young Frankenstein.

00:46:04.770 --> 00:46:08.990
Give the servants some champagne. This stuff's wasted on us.

00:46:10.110 --> 00:46:11.550
Well, well, well, well.

00:46:14.950 --> 00:46:17.830
Go on, mop it up, mop it up, it'll do you good.

00:46:18.220 --> 00:46:19.320
House of Frankenstein.

00:46:19.700 --> 00:46:20.940
House of Frankenstein.

00:46:21.140 --> 00:46:21.640
Thank you.

00:46:22.500 --> 00:46:24.860
Now then, now be off about your business.

00:46:52.200 --> 00:46:56.700
It's extraordinary how friendly you can make a lot of people on a couple of bottles of beer.

00:46:57.760 --> 00:46:59.860
Tomorrow, tomorrow they'll all be fighting.

00:47:02.240 --> 00:47:03.600
They're calling for you, ma'am.

00:47:04.380 --> 00:47:06.840
Well, I suppose I'd better show myself.

00:47:09.040 --> 00:47:17.290
Thank you all very much indeed.

00:47:18.160 --> 00:47:19.660
I'm very pleased to see you all,

00:47:20.010 --> 00:47:22.290
and I hope there's plenty of beer at all of us.

00:47:22.410 --> 00:47:23.650
There's lots more where that came from.

00:48:00.030 --> 00:48:03.220
You stay here, Maria. I'll just take a look at my traps.

00:48:03.740 --> 00:48:05.700
Never go to the village and have a grand time, huh?

00:48:06.240 --> 00:48:09.230
It won't be long, Daddy. Oh, no, no.

00:48:09.620 --> 00:48:11.160
If France goes by, tell him I'll be back soon.

00:48:11.520 --> 00:48:15.090
Daddy, won't you stay and play with me a little while?

00:48:15.610 --> 00:48:19.350
I'm too busy, darling. You stay and play with the kitty, huh?

00:48:21.030 --> 00:48:21.630
Bye, Daddy.

00:48:22.340 --> 00:48:24.340
Goodbye. Be a good girl now.

00:48:26.510 --> 00:48:26.730
Kitty?

00:48:32.520 --> 00:48:32.900
Three

00:49:00.030 --> 00:49:20.650
Will you play with me? Would you like one of my flowers?

00:49:34.640 --> 00:49:47.380
And I'll be.

00:50:00.250 --> 00:50:01.210
See how mine floats?

00:50:30.830 --> 00:50:31.090
I Gãy subscribe cho kênh Ghiền Mì Gõ Để không bỏ lỡ những video hấp dẫn

00:51:00.000 --> 00:51:00.240
Thank you.

00:51:34.030 --> 00:51:34.430
Henry.

00:51:36.490 --> 00:51:36.890
Elizabeth.

00:51:38.390 --> 00:51:39.750
Oh, how lovely you look.

00:51:40.300 --> 00:51:41.220
But you shouldn't be here.

00:51:41.620 --> 00:51:42.880
I must see you for a minute.

00:51:46.390 --> 00:51:48.730
Why, what's the matter?

00:51:55.010 --> 00:51:56.150
Could you leave us for a moment?

00:51:57.900 --> 00:51:58.700
Why, of course.

00:52:08.220 --> 00:52:09.220
What is it?

00:52:09.220 --> 00:52:10.220
I'm so glad you're safe.

00:52:10.220 --> 00:52:11.220
Safe?

00:52:11.220 --> 00:52:12.220
Of course I'm safe.

00:52:12.796 --> 00:52:13.556
But you look worried.

00:52:14.364 --> 00:52:15.364
Is anything wrong?

00:52:15.996 --> 00:52:16.496
No.

00:52:17.788 --> 00:52:18.288
Nope.

00:52:18.336 --> 00:52:19.676
Forget my foolishness.

00:52:20.092 --> 00:52:21.252
It was just a mood.

00:52:21.788 --> 00:52:22.628
There's nothing the matter.

00:52:22.748 --> 00:52:23.948
Of course there isn't.

00:52:24.764 --> 00:52:25.264
Had me.

00:52:26.108 --> 00:52:27.268
I'm afraid...

00:52:27.580 --> 00:52:28.300
Terribly afraid.

00:52:29.276 --> 00:52:29.976
Where's Dr. Bell?

00:52:30.030 --> 00:52:31.070
Why is he late for the wedding?

00:52:31.230 --> 00:52:34.130
Oh, he's always late. He'll be here soon.

00:52:35.560 --> 00:52:38.290
Something is going to happen. Feel it.

00:52:39.440 --> 00:52:40.540
Can't get it out of my mind.

00:52:40.700 --> 00:52:41.980
You're just nervous.

00:52:42.200 --> 00:52:44.650
All the excitement and preparation.

00:52:45.800 --> 00:52:49.810
No, no, it isn't that. I felt it all day.

00:52:49.970 --> 00:52:55.650
Something is coming between us. I know it. I know it.

00:52:55.750 --> 00:52:58.750
Sit down and rest. You look so tired.

00:53:00.732 --> 00:53:02.732
If I could just do something to save us from it.

00:53:02.832 --> 00:53:04.832
From what, dear? From what?

00:53:06.620 --> 00:53:07.180
I don't know.

00:53:08.060 --> 00:53:09.380
If I could just get it out of my mind.

00:53:10.556 --> 00:53:12.256
Oh, I'd die if I had to lose you now, Henry.

00:53:12.416 --> 00:53:13.096
Lose me?

00:53:13.396 --> 00:53:14.776
Why, I'll always be with you.

00:53:15.612 --> 00:53:16.612
Will you, Henry?

00:53:17.116 --> 00:53:17.736
Are you sure?

00:53:19.452 --> 00:53:20.352
I love you so.

00:53:21.820 --> 00:53:23.820
shot.

00:53:23.932 --> 00:53:25.052
How beautiful you look.

00:53:30.320 --> 00:53:30.600
What's that?

00:53:30.960 --> 00:53:31.360
Henry!

00:53:31.850 --> 00:53:33.110
Dr. Baalman!

00:53:33.250 --> 00:53:34.840
All about Dr. Baalman!

00:53:35.490 --> 00:53:36.490
Henry, don't leave!

00:53:36.690 --> 00:53:37.370
Don't leave me!

00:53:37.590 --> 00:53:38.590
No, darling, you stay here.

00:53:39.790 --> 00:53:40.590
Henry, please!

00:53:41.320 --> 00:53:43.140
Dr. Baalman's been murdered in the tower!

00:53:43.340 --> 00:53:44.340
It's a monster!

00:53:44.520 --> 00:53:44.980
He's been murdered!

00:53:45.000 --> 00:53:46.640
I've been seen in the hills terrorizing the mountainside.

00:53:47.900 --> 00:53:52.130
He's in the house, he's upstairs!

00:55:00.828 --> 00:55:01.328
All right.

00:55:35.820 --> 00:55:37.600
Let it come here!

00:55:38.020 --> 00:55:39.250
Let it come here!

00:56:00.000 --> 00:56:00.040
Thank you.

00:56:41.040 --> 00:56:41.560
Thank you.

00:57:02.780 --> 00:57:04.580
What is it? What is it?

00:57:05.420 --> 00:57:07.660
Maria, she's drowned.

00:57:09.270 --> 00:57:12.350
My poor man, why do you bring her here to me?

00:57:13.210 --> 00:57:14.660
But she's been murdered!

00:57:15.000 --> 00:57:24.460
You see the justice is done? Who is it?

00:57:35.020 --> 00:57:35.800
How is Elizabeth now?

00:57:36.250 --> 00:57:38.950
I don't know. She's still in a daze.

00:57:39.210 --> 00:57:40.790
Just looks at me and says nothing.

00:57:41.630 --> 00:57:43.690
It's mad. Easy, old man. She'll be all right.

00:57:44.410 --> 00:57:45.970
Our wedding day. Steady.

00:57:46.600 --> 00:57:48.500
The wedding will only be postponed a day at most.

00:57:48.700 --> 00:57:51.000
A day? I wonder.

00:57:51.850 --> 00:57:52.350
What do you mean?

00:57:52.570 --> 00:57:56.190
There can be no wedding while this horrible creation of mine is still alive.

00:57:56.920 --> 00:57:59.980
I made him with these hands, and with these hands I will destroy him.

00:58:00.480 --> 00:58:01.320
I must find him.

00:58:01.480 --> 00:58:02.120
I'll go with you.

00:58:02.280 --> 00:58:04.310
No, you stay here and look after Elizabeth.

00:58:05.500 --> 00:58:07.990
I leave her in your care, whatever happens.

00:58:08.570 --> 00:58:09.050
You understand?

00:58:09.920 --> 00:58:10.740
In your care.

00:58:25.100 --> 00:58:25.920
That's the woods.

00:58:26.020 --> 00:58:26.800
Those are your group.

00:58:31.760 --> 00:58:36.650
Frankenstein, you will take to the mountains. Those are your people.

00:58:38.600 --> 00:58:41.620
We will lead the third group by the lake.

00:58:43.920 --> 00:58:48.010
Remember, get him alive if you can, but get him!

00:58:50.940 --> 00:58:54.840
Search every ravine, every crevice, but

00:58:54.840 --> 00:58:56.660
the fiend must be found!

00:59:02.010 --> 00:59:02.610
Go

01:00:09.370 --> 01:00:11.270
Frankenstein Motins!

01:00:11.470 --> 01:00:12.530
Don't move on!

01:00:13.290 --> 01:00:15.450
Wake his way!

01:00:59.120 --> 01:00:59.260
Very well.

01:01:37.660 --> 01:01:39.680
Which way did he go? Tell me! Tell me!

01:01:40.970 --> 01:01:42.910
You stay here and take care of him.

01:01:43.370 --> 01:01:44.900
The rest follow me. Come on!

01:01:45.300 --> 01:01:47.260
Come on, quick! Come on!

01:02:07.580 --> 01:02:09.770
Come back this way.

01:02:30.860 --> 01:02:31.740
I think he's up there.

01:02:31.900 --> 01:02:32.840
Come on, follow him.

01:02:33.040 --> 01:02:33.440
Follow him.

01:02:33.890 --> 01:02:34.090
Quick!

01:02:55.330 --> 01:02:55.770
Ha!

01:02:56.650 --> 01:02:56.890
Ha!

01:03:02.460 --> 01:03:08.100
Listen, it's Frankenstein.

01:03:09.040 --> 01:03:09.600
That way!

01:03:30.570 --> 01:03:36.390
Wait! Wait! Wait! Come on!

01:04:32.330 --> 01:04:32.630
Thank you.

01:06:15.600 --> 01:06:25.290
Frankenstein, bring him down to the village and let's take him home.

01:06:30.000 --> 01:06:30.200
You

01:08:08.480 --> 01:08:13.080
Why, why, well, go ahead now.

01:08:21.800 --> 01:08:24.550
What's all this? What do you want, eh?

01:08:25.070 --> 01:08:26.900
What, what's this?

01:08:27.720 --> 01:08:28.960
If you please, Herr Baron.

01:08:30.000 --> 01:08:33.160
What do you thought that Mr. Henry could do with the glass of his great-grandmother's wine?

01:08:34.660 --> 01:08:36.740
Fine old lady, my grandmother.

01:08:38.760 --> 01:08:40.280
Very foreseeing of her.

01:08:40.710 --> 01:08:42.970
To prevent my grandfather drinking this.

01:08:51.060 --> 01:08:53.220
Mr. Henry doesn't need this.

01:08:53.820 --> 01:08:57.640
Well, as I said before, I say again.

01:08:58.540 --> 01:08:59.960
Here's, here's to...

01:09:00.000 --> 01:09:02.520
to your son to the house of Frankenstein.

01:09:03.060 --> 01:09:03.880
Leave, sir.

01:09:04.180 --> 01:09:04.740
Leave, sir.
